:false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":2978,"state":"closed","created_at":"2025-05-22T16:25:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T16:23:23Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-01-26T18:09:14Z"},"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-06-19T09:43:54Z","updated_at":"2025-10-06T14:17:01Z","closed_at":"2025-10-06T14:13:09Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.4.1\n- *Not* Reproducable in 4.3.0\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Solus 4.7 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 Ti (nvidia; 570.153.02) - AMD Ryzen 9 5950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI noticed that FSR 2.2 is doing _something_ above native res in 4.4.1. I can see some edges dancing that do not in Bilinear or FSR 1 mode.\n\nAt scaling factor 1.0x TAA cleans up these glittery artifacts pretty well, but the TAA turns off above full res.\n\nIn the MRP it is more obvious than in my own project - everything is jittering around very noticeably.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Use a simple model with hard lines to better show the aliasing artifacts\n2. Set `set_scaling_3d_scale(1.25)` (most visible in this range but still present at higher scales)\n3. Set `set_scaling_3d_mode(Viewport.SCALING_3D_MODE_FSR2)`\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[reproducing_fsr_bug_2025-06-19_04-40-42.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20816079/reproducing_fsr_bug_2025-06-19_04-40-42.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo